<title>PHILIPPINES: Bell Helicopter to invest in Philippines.</title>
<headline>Bell Helicopter to invest in Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Bell Helicopter Textron has chosen the Philippines as its regional base in Asia, the presidential palace said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Bell Helicopter president Lloyd Shoppa told Philippine President Fidel Ramos of his company's plans to set up a helicopter body and parts manufacturing plant in Alaminos, Pangasinan, in northern Philippines, the statement said.</p>
<p>The presidential palace did not say how much Bell Helicopter is investing in the Philippines.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
